theorem linear-function-inverse
  note        Book of Proof 12.5.5. The inverse of f(x) = πx − e is
              g(x) = (x + e)/π; the two compositions are the identity.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  then (π·x − e + e)/π = x and π·((x + e)/π) − e = x

1.  0 < π
    real arithmetic

2.  (π·x − e + e)/π = x
    algebra
    requires 0 ≠ π: weakening, from 1

3.  π·((x + e)/π) − e = x
    algebra
    requires 0 ≠ π: weakening, from 1

4.  (π·x − e + e)/π = x. π·((x + e)/π) − e = x.
    join 2, 3
